---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="About this engineering notebook.">
	<div class="prose">
		<p class="kicker">About</p>
		<h1>Build things. Write down why.</h1>
		<p>
			This notebook documents systems I actually build and investigate: data platforms, AI agents,
			developer tools, and the occasional financial planner. Each entry is backed by code, tests,
			or measurements — inferences are labeled, failures are kept, and "not measured" means
			exactly that.
		</p>
		<h2>Focus areas</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Data engineering — Spark, Databricks, pipelines, migrations</li>
			<li>AI and agents — LLM systems, memory, evaluation, tooling</li>
			<li>Systems and architecture — storage, sync, offline-first design</li>
			<li>Developer tools — scanners, notebooks, automation that compounds</li>
		</ul>
		<h2>Elsewhere</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<a href="https://github.com/xmirtunjay" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="/engineering-notebook/rss.xml">RSS</a>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<h2>How this site is built</h2>
		<p>
			Astro, static generation, GitHub Pages. Content lives in typed collections; case studies
			are generated from repository evidence, never invented. The full inventory pipeline and
			content tooling are part of the story, not hidden behind it.
		</p>
		<p>
			Performance budget, measured from the production build: homepage 11 KB HTML, heaviest
			case-study page 40 KB HTML, all images lazy-loaded, Mermaid and its diagram dependencies
			loaded on demand only on pages that contain diagrams. One demo video (1 MB) is the
			largest asset on the site; everything else is text.
		</p>
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	.kicker {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		color: var(--accent);
		font-weight: 700;
		margin: 0 0 0.5em 0;
	}
</style>
